--- a/docs/eval_harness_design.md
+++ b/docs/eval_harness_design.md
@@ -14,6 +14,15 @@
 - Report generation: structured JSON + Markdown summaries.
 - CLI command `frai eval` wrapping the core harness.
 
+## Thresholds (CI Gating)
+- CLI option `--threshold <metric>=<min>` (can be specified multiple times) gates the eval on metric scores.
+- A threshold passes when the metric's score is at least the minimum. If a metric has no score, the threshold fails.
+- Exit code 0 when all thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified), exit 1 if any fail, exit 2 for malformed thresholds.
+- JSON reports include a top-level `passed` field and `thresholds` list with each threshold's outcome.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL for each threshold.
+- SDK: `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`) and adds the same fields to reports.
+- Thresholds work with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`.
+
 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
